From 4f4b75bb18de1a3353a4cc1f8673df990bcf81a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:13:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(2d): cut a stock open run one radius off by its side

A Contour on an open run picked on the stock rode the run with the
tool centre, so the tool took one radius off the model beside it.

The run now goes through contour_open_run_sided: the tool centre
stands one tool radius plus the stock to leave off the run, on the
side Side names (Outside off the stock, Inside into it, Auto away
from the part). Refused by name: no stock beside the run for
Inside/Outside; no part, or the part on both sides, for Auto; a
tool that would enter the part; a folding offset. The note "Side
does not apply to open runs" now shows only for part picks.

Fixes #1928

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
